In `store.js.es6` the singular `_id` path still deletes the raw foreign key **only inside** the `if (hydrated)` guard:

```js
} else {
  const hydrated = self._lookupSubType(subType, type, obj[k], root);
  if (hydrated) {
    obj[subType] = hydrated;
    delete obj[k];
  }
}
```

So the described change (“moves `delete obj[k]` out of the guard so it deletes even when hydration returns null”) is contradicted by the diff. (It’s true there’s no explicit test for the failed-hydration branch, but the claimed key-drop regression mechanism does not exist here.)
